TigerAI Sustainable Use License (DRAFT - pending legal review / 草稿,待法律審閱)
================================================================

STATUS: draft text for discussion. It has not been reviewed by a lawyer and must
not be treated as final. It is written to have the same intent as the
"Sustainable Use License" used by n8n (modelled on that idea: free to use and
modify, including inside a company, but not to resell or offer as a hosted
service); the wording below is our own, not a copy.

This licence covers the files under the directory `tigerai/` and the small
`TG-HOOK` call sites this project adds to otherwise unmodified upstream files
(those upstream files stay under the upstream MIT licence, see /LICENSE).

1. Grant
   Subject to these terms, the licensor grants you a non-exclusive,
   non-transferable, royalty-free licence to use, copy, modify and run the
   software, and to share it with others, for your own internal business
   purposes or for personal and non-commercial purposes.

2. What you may not do
   a. Sell, resell, sublicense or otherwise make the software, or a modified
      version of it, available to third parties for a fee or other consideration.
   b. Offer the software, or a modified version of it, to third parties as a
      hosted, managed or software-as-a-service product, or as a substantial
      part of one, where the value of that product comes from the software.
   c. Remove or hide licence, copyright or attribution notices.
   d. Use the names "TigerAI" or "OpenAgent Portal", or the logo, other than
      to truthfully say that something is based on or compatible with the
      software. No trademark right is granted (see TRADEMARK.md).

3. Sharing
   You may pass copies on free of charge, for non-commercial purposes only, and
   only together with this licence.

4. Enterprise files
   Files and directories whose name contains ".ee" (for example `*.ee.ts` or a
   directory named `ee/`) are NOT covered by this licence. They are under the
   separate TigerAI Enterprise licence and need a valid subscription to use in
   production. This repository contains none of them; see LICENSE_EE.md.

5. Contributions
   Contributions are accepted under the contributor's sign-off of the Developer
   Certificate of Origin (a "Signed-off-by" line) and are licensed under this
   licence. (Open question for the founder: DCO or a CLA; see docs/DECISIONS.md.)

6. No warranty and no liability
   The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the extent
   permitted by law the licensor is not liable for any damages arising from its
   use.

7. Termination
   Your rights end automatically if you breach these terms, and return if you
   stop and cure the breach within 30 days of becoming aware of it.
